# Block test setup — copy to .env and fill in your own values.
# This file is a template only. NEVER commit your real .env: it holds your
# account password and your site's editor entry. Each person keeps their own
# .env on their own machine; nothing here is shared.
#
# How to get each value (the agent walks you through this on first run):
# - PLAYWRIGHT_USERNAME / PLAYWRIGHT_PASSWORD: your Leadong account.
#   The password is only read by the login script and the runner; it is never
#   printed, logged, or written to any report.
# - EDIT_SITE_URL: your test site's editor entry. After the first login the
#   agent lists your sites; pick yours and it saves the entry URL here.
# - SITE_DOMAIN: the Leadong platform domain. Leave as-is unless your
#   platform host differs.
# - HTTPS_PROXY: only if your test environment needs an HTTP proxy to reach
#   the site (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:7890). Leave empty for direct access.
# - BLOCK_ID: the block under test (its data-appid in the editor).
# - TARGET_PAGE: the page to test on (default products). The first-run setup
#   records the choice in the block's profile instead; this is only an
#   override for one-off runs.
# - FIGMA_TOKEN: optional, only if your agent has no Figma connector.
#   Without it, style checks are skipped with a note. Create one at
#   Figma → Settings → Security → Personal access tokens.
# - STORAGE_STATE: optional override for the login-session file. Default is
#   src/fixtures/storageState-<account>.json, created by the login script.

PLAYWRIGHT_USERNAME=
PLAYWRIGHT_PASSWORD=
EDIT_SITE_URL=
SITE_DOMAIN=https://www.leadong.com
HTTPS_PROXY=
BLOCK_ID=
TARGET_PAGE=products
FIGMA_TOKEN=
STORAGE_STATE=
